{
  "description": "an on_key handler body runs in the environment captured at REGISTRATION, not the one current when the key is delivered. The handler is registered inside setup and fires from the top-level wait, after setup has returned, so :v exists only in the registration environment - printing 7 is possible only if that environment was captured and used, and resolving against the delivery-time scope raises ol-undefined-var instead. Companion to every-body-runs-in-registration-environment (issue #828): that fixture was added after a regression in invokeEveryHandler survived the whole corpus precisely because this property was asserted nowhere, and the same mutation applied to on_key was likewise survivable until this fixture existed. Pins capture of the ENVIRONMENT, which is weaker than capturing values: nothing is snapshotted and no fresh bindings are made, which is why issue #821's loop case is still open",
